# Round 113: return_node_is_boxed presumed an INDEX-READ return numeric
# (index nodes fell through to "not boxed"), while is_num_expr's index
# arm says NOT numeric unless the target is a numeric C buffer. The two
# inferences disagreed at exactly the boundary CLAUDE.md warns about: a
# string-table lookup function was declared `static double`, its return
# died through aot_num_ck_at, and the CALLER's accumulator was typed
# numeric off the "numeric" callee -- `s is s + pick1 of x` died
# "non-numeric value in a numeric context: name s (type str)" rc 1
# where the VM runs. The same expression INLINE was already correct;
# the defect was only the return-position consumer of "what class is a
# list element?" -- the #178 family's return member.
#
# Second half, one level up: `+` is the one polymorphic binop, and
# return_node_is_boxed had NO arm for it -- chain_has_str catches only
# a string LITERAL, so `return HEXD[a] + HEXD[b]` (no literal, both
# sides boxed lookups) also fell through to double.
#
# Reach: tidelog/test/test_cbor.eigs byte_hex is exactly that second
# shape, and it blocked the ENTIRE RFC 8949 CBOR vector suite -- the VM
# prints "cbor: 73 passed, 0 failed" rc 0, the AOT died rc 1 before
# printing anything. Verified end-to-end after the fix (2,000+ line
# concatenated probe). EigenMiniSat's full CDCL differential (first
# ever, 2,152 lines, 4 CNFs, all counters and models byte-identical)
# re-verified as the regression control.
#
# Discriminators per invariant 22: bare lookup return, two-lookup
# concat return, nested-list element, dict element -- and the NUMERIC
# BUFFER element return as the control that must STAY double (the
# C-buffer fast path t22's matmul win rides on).
HEXD is ["a", "b", "c", "d"]
define pick1(b) as:
    return HEXD[b]
define go(x) as:
    local s is ""
    s is s + pick1 of x
    return s
print of (go of 2)
define byte_hex(b) as:
    return HEXD[floor of (b / 2)] + HEXD[b % 2]
print of (byte_hex of 5)
NEST is [[10, "x"], [20, "y"]]
define pick_nested(i, j) as:
    return NEST[i][j]
print of (pick_nested of [1, 1])
D is {"k": "vee"}
define pick_dict(k) as:
    return D[k]
print of (pick_dict of "k")
bufv is buffer of 3
bufv[0] is 7
bufv[1] is 8
bufv[2] is 9
define pick_buf(i) as:
    return bufv[i]
print of ((pick_buf of 1) + 1)
# Third half, found while fixing: a Value*-returning user call in a
# forced-numeric context (`1 + (sfn of 3)`) emitted the RAW typed call
# into a double -- uncompilable C, no AOT: line -- even in a DEAD branch
# the VM never executes. Now routed through the checked unbox: this
# branch builds and never fires.
define sfn(x) as:
    return "s" + (str of x)
if 1 == 2:
    print of (1 + (sfn of 3))
print of "done"
